hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"498","Harun ibn Abbad al-Azdi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a writing on the ground and said to a youth with him: What is this? He said: In the name of Allah. He said: May Allah curse whoever did this, and do not place the name of Allah except in its proper place. He said: Then I saw Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz see a son of his write the remembrance of Allah on the wall and he struck him."
"499","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The spider is a devil, so kill it."
